{
  "title": "WorkArena++: Towards Compositional Planning and Reasoning-based Common Knowledge Work Tasks",
  "authors": [
    "L\u00e9o Boisvert",
    "Megh Thakkar",
    "Maxime Gasse",
    "Massimo Caccia",
    "Thibault Le Sellier De Chezelles",
    "Quentin Cappart",
    "Nicolas Chapados",
    "Alexandre Lacoste",
    "Alexandre Drouin"
  ],
  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2407.05291",
  "abstract": "WorkArena++ is a novel benchmark for evaluating the capabilities of web agents in solving complex knowledge work tasks. It consists of 682 tasks that require skills like planning, problem-solving, logical and arithmetic reasoning, and memorization. The benchmark is designed to assess the ability of web agents to perform tasks that mimic real-world enterprise scenarios, providing a valuable tool for evaluating and improving autonomous agents.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Imagine a future where autonomous assistants, or AI agents, handle tedious tasks like searching for information, coordinating group discussions, or filling expense reports. Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have made this future seem possible. However, the ability of LLMs to apply their planning and reasoning capabilities to autonomous task solving remains underexplored. <strong>WorkArena++</strong> aims to fill this gap by providing a benchmark to evaluate the planning, problem-solving, logical and arithmetic reasoning, retrieval, and contextual understanding abilities of web agents.",
